#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# horner_form

#% text
# `horner_form(p)` writes the polynomial `p` in nested (Horner) form; `horner_form(p, x)` or `horner_form(p, [x, y])` chooses the variables, nested in order. A quotient has numerator and denominator done separately.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
horner_form(1 + 2*x + 3*x^2)
#% output
#= 1 + x*(2 + 3*x)

#% cell
horner_form(x^3 + 1)
#% output
#= 1 + x^3

#% cell
horner_form(1 + 2*x + 3*x*y + y^2, [x, y])
#% output
#= 1 + x*(2 + 3*y) + y^2

